      body: 'The Equality Act 2010 protects nine characteristics: age, disability, gender reassignment, marriage and civil partnership, pregnancy and maternity, race, religion or belief, sex, and sexual orientation.\n\nProtection applies at every stage of employment — advertising, recruitment, terms, promotion, training, dismissal and after employment ends, for example in references.'
